# Enrichment for Kindergarten. quiz: "question|a|b|c|d|index|why"
E = {
'K-1-1': dict(teach=['Children this age understand “father” as the person who cares for them. Keep it warm and concrete; avoid abstract words like “omnipotent.”','Use the child’s own experience: someone who feeds them, holds them, keeps them safe. Then say, “God is like that, and even more.”','If a child’s father is absent or unkind, say “God is the best Father” and speak of God’s care without insisting on comparisons.'],
  talk=['Who takes care of you at home?','What does your family do when someone is sad?','What would you like to tell God today?'],
  quiz=['Who is our Father in heaven?|A king far away|God|A statue|Nobody|1|God is our loving Father.','God loves…|Only good children|Only adults|Everyone|Only the strong|2|God loves every person.'],
  life='At bedtime this week, say together: “God, thank you for loving us.”', saint='Thérèse of Lisieux: a little girl who loved God as her Father and trusted him in everything.'),
'K-1-2': dict(teach=['Read Genesis 1 in short pieces, pausing after each day: “And God saw that it was good.” Let children repeat that line.','Keep science and faith together simply: God made the world; how it grew is a question for scientists.','Bring a plant, a shell or a stone so children can touch what God made.'],
  talk=['What did God make that you can see right now?','Why do you think God made so many animals?','How can we take care of what God made?'],
  quiz=['Who made the sky, sea and animals?|God|People|Nobody|The wind|0|God is the Creator.','What did God say about what he made?|It is bad|It is good|It is boring|Nothing|1|Genesis 1.'],
  life='Take a walk with your family and say “thank you, God” for three things you see.', saint='Francis of Assisi: he called the sun, the moon and the animals his brothers and sisters because God made them all.', mem='Genesis 1:31'),
'K-1-3': dict(teach=['Say clearly: “You are not a mistake. God wanted you.” Some children need to hear this.','The “image of God” can be taught as “God made us able to love, think and choose.”','Avoid comparing children; stress that each is unique.'],
  talk=['What are you good at?','What makes you different from your friend?','How can you show love to someone today?'],
  quiz=['Who made you?|God|The wind|A machine|Nobody|0|God made each person.','God made people to…|Know him and love him|Fight|Be alone|Be perfect|0|CCC 356.'],
  life='Look in a mirror and say, “God made me and loves me.” Do it for five days.', saint='Bl. Carlo Acutis: a boy who loved God and computers and showed that everyone has gifts.'),
'K-2-1': dict(teach=['Use a doll or picture of baby Jesus. Children can hold a doll gently and say, “Jesus, welcome.”','Keep to the Gospel: the birth in Bethlehem, Mary, Joseph, the shepherds. Avoid adding details not in Scripture.','Point out that Jesus is both God and a real baby: “God came close to us.”'],
  talk=['How do we take care of a baby?','Who came to visit Jesus?','Why do you think God sent his Son as a baby?'],
  quiz=['Who was Jesus’s mother?|Mary|Martha|Anna|Elizabeth|0|Luke 2.','Where was Jesus born?|Bethlehem|Egypt|Rome|Nazareth|0|Luke 2:4-7.'],
  life='Put a small crib scene where your family can see it and say “Welcome, Jesus” each night.', saint='Francis of Assisi: he made the first living nativity scene to help people see how Jesus was born.', mem='Luke 2:11'),
'K-2-2': dict(teach=['Act out the story: the children sit as a crowd; you pretend to be Jesus; they can gently say “Let them come.”','Use Mark 10:16: “He took them in his arms and blessed them.”','Stress that Jesus is happy to see children and never too busy for them.'],
  talk=['How did the children feel when Jesus hugged them?','What do you want to say to Jesus?','How can you be kind to the little children at your house?'],
  quiz=['What did Jesus do with the children?|Sent them away|Blessed them|Ignored them|Scolded them|1|Mark 10:16.','Jesus loves…|Only grown-ups|Children too|Nobody|Only good children|1|Jesus welcomes children.'],
  life='Give someone at home a hug and say “Jesus loves you.”', saint='Bl. Laura Vicuña: a young girl who loved Jesus and prayed for her mother.'),
'K-2-3': dict(teach=['Choose a story children can picture: Peter’s mother-in-law, the leper who thanks Jesus. Keep illness simple, not scary.','Teach the idea that Jesus heals bodies and hearts, and that he still helps us through doctors, nurses, prayer and the sacraments.','Allow a child to say if someone in their family is sick; pray for them.'],
  talk=['Who do you know who is sick?','How can we help them?','Why did only one man come back to say thank you?'],
  quiz=['Jesus helps people who are…|Strong|Sick and sad|Rich|Famous|1|Mark 1:29-34.','When Jesus helps us, we say…|Nothing|Thank you|Go away|Later|1|Luke 17:15-16.'],
  life='Pray this week for someone who is sick, and make them a card.', saint='Damien of Molokai: a priest who cared for people with leprosy.'),
'K-3-1': dict(teach=['Keep the Annunciation short: an angel, Mary says yes, Jesus will be born.','Show Mary as a young woman who trusts God. “Yes, God” is a prayer even a five-year-old can pray.','Teach the first line of the Hail Mary with hand motions.'],
  talk=['What did Mary say to the angel?','When did you say “yes” to someone who asked for help?','What do you do when your mom asks you to help?'],
  quiz=['Who told Mary she would be Jesus’s mother?|An angel|A shepherd|A neighbor|A king|0|Luke 1:26-38.','What did Mary say to God?|No|Yes|Maybe|Nothing|1|Luke 1:38.'],
  life='This week, when someone asks for help, say “Yes!” with a smile and think of Mary.', saint='Juan Diego: he said yes when Mary asked him to carry her message.', mem='Luke 1:38'),
'K-3-2': dict(teach=['Introduce saints as God’s friends who lived long ago or recently, and who now pray for us.','Show pictures: St Francis, St Thérèse, St Patrick, St Nicholas. Tell one fact about each.','Avoid scary details (martyrdom) in kindergarten.'],
  talk=['Which saint is your favorite?','What can we do to be like the saints?','Why does Jesus want us to be friends with the saints?'],
  quiz=['Saints are…|God’s friends|Strangers|Make-believe|Only old people|0|Saints love God and are with him.','Saints pray for…|Us|Nobody|Only priests|Only kings|0|Hebrews 12:1.'],
  life='Choose a saint for the year and put a picture where your family can see it.', saint='Nicholas: a kind bishop who gave gifts secretly to people in need.'),
'K-3-3': dict(teach=['Say simply: “God sends angels to help us. Each one of us has a guardian angel.”','Teach the guardian angel prayer one line at a time with gestures.','Do not describe angels as babies with wings; they are powerful spirits, but God’s servants who care for us.'],
  talk=['How could an angel help you?','When can we say thank you to our angels?','How is an angel like a helper at home?'],
  quiz=['Who is with us all the time to help?|A guardian angel|A cartoon|A monster|A king|0|CCC 336.','Angels serve…|God|Only kings|Nobody|Pets|0|Psalm 91:11.'],
  life='Say the guardian angel prayer at bedtime this week.', saint='Padre Pio: he said, “Our guardian angel is always with us,” and asked people to send their angel.'),
'K-4-1': dict(teach=['Define “church” in two senses: God’s people and the building. Say both.','Use a family photo: each person is part of one family; the Church is God’s big family.','Introduce baptism as the way we join God’s family.'],
  talk=['Who is in your church family?','Who helps us at church?','Why do we call it God’s family?'],
  quiz=['The Church is…|God’s family|A shop|A zoo|A game|0|CCC 751.','We join God’s family by…|Baptism|Winning|Buying|Wishing|0|CCC 1213.'],
  life='Greet someone at church by name this week.', saint='Mother Teresa: she cared for people everyone else forgot, as a mother cares for her family.'),
'K-4-2': dict(teach=['Teach the vocabulary by pointing: altar, tabernacle (with the red light), cross, holy water.','Practice: dip fingers, make the Sign of the Cross, genuflect to the tabernacle, sit quietly.','Say why we are quiet: because Jesus is there.'],
  talk=['What do you see in our church?','Why do we make the Sign of the Cross?','How do we show respect for Jesus?'],
  quiz=['Where is Jesus kept in church?|In the tabernacle|In the car|At home|In a book|0|CCC 1379.','Holy water reminds us of…|Our Baptism|A swimming pool|Rain|A drink|0|CCC 1668.'],
  life='Visit the church with a grown-up and look for the cross, the altar and the tabernacle.', saint='Tarcisius: a boy who carried Jesus in the Eucharist and protected him.'),
'K-4-3': dict(teach=['Mass is “the family meal of God’s family.” We listen, we thank, we receive.','Use pictures to show the parts: gathering, listening, thanking, sharing, going out.','Practice “Amen” and “Thanks be to God.”'],
  talk=['What do you like about Mass?','What do we do when we gather?','How do we get ready for Sunday?'],
  quiz=['On Sunday, Christians go to…|Mass|The mall|A race|Work|0|CCC 2177.','Sunday celebrates…|The day Jesus rose|A birthday|A holiday for toys|Nothing|0|CCC 1166.'],
  life='Lay out your “Mass clothes” on Saturday night with your family.', saint='Bl. Imelda: a girl who loved Jesus in the Eucharist so much that she longed to receive him.'),
'K-5-1': dict(teach=['Bring a baptism candle and a shell. Let children handle them.','Explain: water, words, oil, white garment, candle. “We are God’s children.”','Do not focus on the fear of sin; focus on welcome and new life.'],
  talk=['Do you know your baptism day?','What did they give you? (A white garment, a candle.)','Who are your godparents?'],
  quiz=['In Baptism we get…|Water and God’s life|A new toy|A car|A cake|0|CCC 1214-1216.','Baptism makes us…|God’s children|Strangers|Kings|Soldiers|0|CCC 1265.'],
  life='Ask your parents to tell the story of your baptism day. Look at the photos.', saint='Lucy: a girl who stayed faithful to Christ; her name means light, like the baptismal candle.'),
'K-5-2': dict(teach=['Teach with reverence, not fear. “At Mass, bread and wine become Jesus. We wait to receive him when we are older, and we love him now.”','Never imply the child has done anything wrong by not receiving yet.','Practice a quiet bow and “Jesus, I love you.”'],
  talk=['How do we show love for Jesus at Mass?','What can you say to Jesus in your heart?','Why do we kneel?'],
  quiz=['At Mass, bread and wine become…|Jesus|Candy|Water|A symbol only|0|CCC 1376.','We show respect by…|Being quiet and kind|Shouting|Playing|Running|0|Reverence.'],
  life='Make a quiet “thank you, Jesus” card to place in your Bible or prayer corner.', saint='Tarcisius: a young martyr of the Eucharist.'),
'K-5-3': dict(teach=['Keep God’s forgiveness central. Use the story of the lost sheep or the prodigal son.','Teach the simple phrase “I’m sorry. I forgive you.” and practice with partners.','Do not mention specific sins; focus on kindness and mistakes children understand.'],
  talk=['What did you do when you hurt someone?','How did it feel when someone forgave you?','What does God do when we say sorry?'],
  quiz=['When we do wrong, God…|Forgets us|Is ready to forgive|Is angry forever|Leaves|1|CCC 1439.','We say…|“I’m sorry”|“Whatever”|“You’re wrong”|Nothing|0|Reconciliation.'],
  life='This week say “I’m sorry” the moment you hurt someone.', saint='Maria Goretti: a girl who forgave as she was dying.'),
'K-6-1': dict(teach=['Teach the Golden Rule as an action: “Do for others what you would like.”','Use role play with puppets: one shares, one does not; ask “How would you feel?”','Link to Jesus: he shows us how.'],
  talk=['How do you like to be treated?','What is one kind thing you did today?','Who needs a friend at school?'],
  quiz=['The Golden Rule says…|Treat others as you want to be treated|Be first|Win|Hide|0|Matthew 7:12.','Jesus wants us to love…|God and our neighbor|Only family|Only friends|Only ourselves|0|Mark 12:30-31.'],
  life='Do one kind thing a day this week; draw a heart each time.', saint='Martin de Porres: a Peruvian friar who loved the poor and animals.'),
'K-6-2': dict(teach=['Define truth as saying what really happened. Tell a short story about a child who tells the truth and feels free.','Keep it positive. Avoid shaming children who have lied.','Teach that God helps us be brave.'],
  talk=['What does it feel like to tell the truth?','Who can you tell when you are afraid to tell the truth?','What does a lie do to a friendship?'],
  quiz=['God wants us to…|Tell the truth|Hide things|Pretend|Lie|0|Exodus 20:16.','When we tell the truth we feel…|Free|Trapped|Sick|Lost|0|John 8:32.'],
  life='Choose one day this week for “truth day”: tell the truth no matter what.', saint='Thomas More: a man who told the truth even when it cost him.'),
'K-6-3': dict(teach=['Practice a simple forgiveness routine with partners. Emphasize that forgiving is a decision to be kind, even when we still feel hurt.','Tell them to tell a trusted adult if someone keeps hurting them.','Link to the Our Father: “forgive us as we forgive.”'],
  talk=['When have you forgiven someone?','What do you say when you want to forgive?','Who forgives us always?'],
  quiz=['When someone says sorry, we can…|Forgive|Hit|Ignore|Tease|0|Matthew 18:21-22.','Jesus forgives us so we can…|Forgive others|Be mean|Keep score|Run away|0|Ephesians 4:32.'],
  life='If someone upsets you this week, say “It’s okay. I forgive you.”', saint='Maria Goretti: she forgave her attacker with her last words.'),
'K-7-1': dict(teach=['Prayer is “talking and listening to God.” Use the image of a phone call to someone who loves you.','Teach simple ways: folded hands, quiet eyes, kneeling, hands open.','Allow a minute of silence; praise children for trying.'],
  talk=['What would you tell God today?','When is it easy to pray?','How do you feel when you pray?'],
  quiz=['Prayer is talking with…|God|The wall|The TV|A phone|0|CCC 2559.','We can pray…|Anywhere|Only at church|Only on Sunday|Never|0|1 Thessalonians 5:17.'],
  life='Pick a time and place for a daily prayer with your family.', saint='Bernadette Soubirous: a girl who prayed the Rosary and saw Our Lady at Lourdes.'),
'K-7-2': dict(teach=['Teach the Our Father with simple gestures: hands up for “heaven,” hands open for “bread,” hands crossed for “forgive.”','Say: “Jesus gave us this prayer. It is the prayer of God’s family.”','Say it slowly; children rush.'],
  talk=['What do you ask for in the Our Father?','What does “daily bread” mean to you?','Who do you forgive?'],
  quiz=['Who taught us the Our Father?|Jesus|A saint|A teacher|A king|0|Matthew 6:9.','The Our Father begins with…|Our Father, who art in heaven|Hail Mary|Lord, have mercy|Glory be|0|CCC 2759.'],
  life='Pray the Our Father before meals this week.', saint='Teresa of Avila: she taught that the Our Father is the best prayer to learn.'),
'K-7-3': dict(teach=['The Sign of the Cross is the shortest creed. Slow it down and trace the cross carefully on the body.','Teach grace before meals: a short, grateful pause. Include a child to lead.','Link to the Trinity: Father, Son, Holy Spirit.'],
  talk=['Why do we pray before eating?','What are you thankful for?','Who made the food?'],
  quiz=['We make the Sign of the Cross to…|Pray in the name of the Trinity|Wave|Scratch|Count|0|CCC 2157.','Before we eat we…|Thank God|Argue|Run|Play|0|Matthew 14:19.'],
  life='Lead grace at one meal each day this week.', saint='Brother Lawrence: a kitchen worker who prayed while washing pots.'),
'K-8-1': dict(teach=['Bring an Advent wreath. Light the candles in order; explain purple and pink.','Teach waiting as active: we prepare our hearts with kind acts.','Sing a simple Advent song.'],
  talk=['What are we waiting for?','How can you get your heart ready?','What helps you wait?'],
  quiz=['Advent is a time to…|Prepare for Jesus’s birth|Hunt eggs|Go to the beach|Fast all day|0|CCC 524.','The candles of Advent are…|Purple and pink|Black|Yellow|Green only|0|Liturgy.'],
  life='Light the Advent candle with your family each evening and say a prayer.', saint='John the Baptist: he told people to get ready for Jesus.'),
'K-8-2': dict(teach=['Lent: small, joyful sacrifices and giving to others. Easter: celebration.','Explain that we do not give up things because they are bad, but to make room for Jesus and the poor.','Decorate a cross or an Easter egg with a cross.'],
  talk=['What can you share this Lent?','Why do we celebrate at Easter?','How can you help someone in need?'],
  quiz=['Easter is when…|Jesus rose from the dead|Jesus was born|The apostles were chosen|The Church began|0|Luke 24.','In Lent we pray, fast and…|Give to the poor|Buy toys|Sleep|Complain|0|Matthew 6:1-18.'],
  life='Put coins in a Lenten box for the poor each week.', saint='Francis of Assisi: he gave up everything to follow Jesus and care for the poor.'),
'K-8-3': dict(teach=['Ordinary Time is green: growing time. Connect to the parables of seeds and plants.','Plant seeds and check them weekly. Link to growing in love.','End with a thank-you prayer.'],
  talk=['What helps a plant grow?','What helps us grow in love?','What are you thankful for?'],
  quiz=['Green is the color of…|Ordinary Time|Lent|Easter|Advent|0|Liturgical colors.','We grow in love by…|Prayer and kindness|Hiding|Fighting|Winning|0|Colossians 3.'],
  life='Water a plant with your family and thank God for the gift of life.', saint='Thérèse of Lisieux: she called herself a “little flower” and taught the little way of love.'),
}
